{:edb/db-before-t 1090 :edb/db-after-t 1091 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534403 50 #inst "2026-10-07T00:33:23.834Z" 13194139534403 true] [17592186096632 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286540 13194139534403 true] [17592186096683 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286547 13194139534403 true] [17592186096684 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286533 13194139534403 true] [17592186096933 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534403 true] [17592186096933 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003808/assets/8b1d78038032973d7bb5738b67963e0bfadb258e4c1eb06f191496bded406696.png)\n\nWhat is the vertex of the parabola shown above?" 13194139534403 true] [17592186096933 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1128/Source/Images/q-11858.png)\n\nWhat is the vertex of the parabola shown above?" 13194139534403 false] [17592186096933 1145 "The vertex of a right-opening parabola is the left-most point of the parabola.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003808/assets/aaf295d69a75c976df8aaf02ee6680486c502f7ce5719b41682cdf2499cab984.png)\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the vertex are $(-6,0).$" 13194139534403 true] [17592186097295 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534403 true] [17592186097295 1100 "What are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola $x^{2} = 4(y - 2)$?" 13194139534403 false] [17592186097295 1100 "What are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola ${x}^{2}=4(y-2)?$" 13194139534403 true] [17592186097295 1145 "The standard equation of an upward- or downward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nComparing our equation with the standard equation, we can see that we have $h=0$ and $k=2.$ Therefore, the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola are $(0,2).$" 13194139534403 true] [17592186286533 1017 #edb/ref 17592186286534 13194139534403 true] [17592186286533 1089 "q-115908" 13194139534403 true] [17592186286533 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534403 true] [17592186286533 1100 "What are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola ${y}^{2}=-32x?$" 13194139534403 true] [17592186286533 1113 #uuid "2b179cc8-ceb4-5e1d-8755-bb1a361af2ed" 13194139534403 true] [17592186286533 1145 "The standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola that has its vertex at the origin is\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant.\n\nWe can rewrite the given equation as \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4(-8)x.\n$$\n\nIt is now clear that our equation is of the standard type with $p=-8.$ Therefore, our parabola has its vertex at $(0,0).$" 13194139534403 true] [17592186286534 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286535 13194139534403 true] [17592186286534 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286536 13194139534403 true] [17592186286534 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286537 13194139534403 true] [17592186286534 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286538 13194139534403 true] [17592186286534 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286539 13194139534403 true] [17592186286534 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534403 true] [17592186286534 1041 "selection" 13194139534403 true] [17592186286534 1104 #edb/ref 17592186286535 13194139534403 true] [17592186286534 1110 #uuid "c11659e4-5655-5354-9e81-acb082c53299" 13194139534403 true] [17592186286535 1034 "(0,0)" 13194139534403 true] [17592186286535 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534403 true] [17592186286535 1111 #uuid "97a079cd-1a5e-56de-9bd6-987023c816da" 13194139534403 true] [17592186286536 1034 "(-32,0)" 13194139534403 true] [17592186286536 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534403 true] [17592186286536 1111 #uuid "82116a47-2385-5ab1-92ef-e669f9784a4d" 13194139534403 true] [17592186286537 1034 "(0,-8)" 13194139534403 true] [17592186286537 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534403 true] [17592186286537 1111 #uuid "a21b34b6-b728-596f-a47f-6c5589f1e1ae" 13194139534403 true] [17592186286538 1034 "(8,0)" 13194139534403 true] [17592186286538 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534403 true] [17592186286538 1111 #uuid "248d0675-1c22-5207-9166-a41b8